@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# Optional plain GPU inventory allowlist (local v0.18.0 patch)
+
+The operator may set an optional **configuration-file-only** field:
+
+```yaml
+version: v1
+flags:
+  migStrategy: none
+  deviceDiscoveryStrategy: nvml
+  plugin:
+    allowedGPUUUIDs:
+      - GPU-16128952-b438-556a-00bb-93039ee24e56
+```
+
+An absent field preserves upstream behavior. Explicit null, a bare key, wrong types,
+a configured empty list, duplicate,
+noncanonical full physical GPU UUID, or UUID absent from the enumerated inventory
+fails startup. The selector accepts only lowercase canonical `GPU-xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx`
+identities; indices, products, prefixes, and MIG identities are rejected.
+
+With a selector, only native NVML discovery (`nvml`, or `auto` resolving to native
+NVML), MIG strategy `none`, no MIG-enabled physical devices, no time-slicing
+resource definitions, and no MPS definition are supported. Errors never fall back
+to unrestricted inventory, including when `failOnInitError` is false. Filtering
+happens before resource managers or kubelet registration. Each allowed physical
+device keeps its original ID, index, health handling, and CDI/environment response
+semantics under the stock `nvidia.com/gpu` resource. No replicas or additional
+sharing owner are introduced.
+
+There is no selector CLI flag, environment variable, or tenant Pod annotation.
+The operator controls the per-node config and must use the same patched image for
+the device plugin and config-manager; the upstream config-manager forwards the
+selected file by symlink without rewriting it. The typed pointer preserves explicit
+empty lists through configuration serialization.
+
+Advertising one of two physical devices changes kubelet capacity and allocatable
+GPU count from two to one. Physical topology/GFD counts may still correctly say
+two. This requires an explicit inventory/authority transition and compatible KAI
+accounting before deployment; existing exact-two qualification evidence cannot
+be reused. This is placement inventory filtering, not device isolation or proof
+of qualification. Expanding the list requires separately qualified devices and
+matching authority/accounting. A singleton pilot does not complete the all-eight
+GPU production acceptance gate.
